{
  "analysis": "No news feed and a negligible drawdown (-0.27%, no forced actions), so this is a pure risk-sizing decision. The dominant feature in the data is dispersion in forecast uncertainty: 5-day 80% interval widths range from 3.5% (A09 bonds) to 11.8% (A07, A01). Since median forecasts carry no directional skill, I size positions off interval width (the reliable signal) and recent volatility, not off median signs. Recent returns are mixed: strong 20d momentum in A05 (+13.5%), A14 (+14.8%), A12 (+10.0%) but negative 1d/5d in A07, A13, A01, A04. Main risks: idiosyncratic volatility in the single stocks (A14 59% ann., A07 42%, A01 33%), group concentration (us_broad ~17%, financials ~14%), and the wide-interval tail names. My stance: keep the existing defensive tilt and formalize it — overweight the narrowest-interval assets (A09 bonds, A06 intl developed) as ballast, stay at zero in the two widest-interval/highest-vol stocks (A01, A07), cap A14 below baseline despite its momentum because its 59% vol and 9.4% interval dominate, and hold cash at ~12.7% (above the 10% floor) since there is no edge in the medians and cash is the asymmetric safe asset. All changes from current weights are under 2pp except none — this is a confirmation, not a churn, rebalance.",
  "positions": [
    {
      "symbol": "A02",
      "target_weight": 0.095,
      "rationale": "Narrow 5d interval (3.95%) and low vol (11.6%) make it a core broad-US holding; target near baseline (9.34%), slight trim from current 10.02% to fund cash.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A11",
      "target_weight": 0.06,
      "rationale": "Tech-growth ETF with moderate interval (5.96%) and 20.6% vol; hold near baseline. Tech group exposure stays modest because A01 is zeroed and A14 is capped.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A10",
      "target_weight": 0.068,
      "rationale": "Broad US ETF, interval 5.54%, vol 14.5%; near baseline (6.67%), tiny trim from current 6.97%.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A06",
      "target_weight": 0.105,
      "rationale": "Second-narrowest 5d interval (4.03%) and low vol (13.2%); overweight vs baseline 9.16% (+1.3pp) as a low-risk diversifier to the US-heavy book. Within the +15pp increase allowance.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A12",
      "target_weight": 0.044,
      "rationale": "Emerging markets: wide interval (8.3%) and 23.7% vol cap the size despite strong 20d momentum (+10%); hold near baseline 4.45%.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
